   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Seefeldstrasse 73</name> <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> VIII: <name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>
                            </addrLine> </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: Your registered letter of<date when="1917-04-04"> 4 instant</date> speaks of 8 enclosures (American reviews of <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my novel</rs>
                        </seg>). It contains however no enclosures. Will you kindly therefore inquire into the matter? The postal number is: Crawford Street P.O. W: R. London W. 21. The <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">censor’s number</seg> is 1378. I am sorry to hear that the sales of <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my novel</rs> are unsatisfactory. My eyes are better now but unfortunately not yet cured. The <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">dozen copies</seg> of <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">the novel</rs> arrived and I shall remit you the amount.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>                    	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>                                	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> </closer>
                </div> </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">
                    <name type="work" key="W_A_PORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">During WWI, incoming letters were opened by British government censors before being forwarded to the intended recipient; these were re-sealed with a sticker indicating the censor’s ID number.</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">On <date when="1917-01-14">14 January 1917</date>, JJ wrote to Harriet Weaver: “Will you also let me know the published price of the English edition and the foreign postage (per dozen copies) so that I may remit you an order for such copies as I buy at trade price? I hope to be able to dispose of a few dozen here” (<name type="work">LII</name> 388).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
